{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And those who turn aside</b> — like <b>ומטי גר ולא יראוני</b>, and the bet is absent, like <b>הנמצאים בית ה'</b>. So too it is <b>והמטים בעקלקלותם</b>: let one pray that HaShem remove them far, and they be with workers of iniquity, with the nations — then there will be peace upon Israel."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 125, :notes {0 "The phrase 'let one pray' renders יתפלל as an impersonal jussive; Ibn Ezra reads verse 5 as a wish rather than a declaration."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:18.402432464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}